{
  "id": "66b0de41-be11-474f-badf-f2b9b934eaf9",
  "featureId": "873f81ba-ce7c-4bcc-90ed-27a25a742285",
  "number": 87,
  "shortId": "E3D3Y",
  "priority": 1,
  "slug": "the-seam-components-and-the-first-extraction",
  "title": "The seam: components/ and the first extraction",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "Create heca/src/components/, fix the contract and the test pattern, and prove both on the highest-frequency composition — the chrome action button.",
  "description": "The folder plus the two rules that decide everything after it, proven on one real extraction rather than asserted in a doc.\n\n## What exists — updated 2026-08-12\n\n**`heca/src/components/mod.rs` EXISTS** (T373, done): the contract and the headless-test pattern, written as the module doc. `mod components;` is in `heca/src/main.rs`. Nothing has moved into it yet.\n\nEverything else is still inline: `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` (5270 lines), `heca/src/providers/workspaces/mod.rs` (2200), `heca/src/chrome/expose.rs` (2028).\n\nThe **chrome action button** is the highest-frequency inline composition and the subject of T374, because AGENTS already documents it as a recipe every caller repeats by hand (AGENTS § \"Chrome buttons → action, tooltip, KeyHint\"):\n\n1. `action_tooltip(button, action_name, label, &state.action_shortcuts)` — `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:633` — composes `\"<label>  <shortcut>\"` from the action's **name**.\n2. `KeyHint::new(w).on_peek(fires(intent, emit))` for the pick + `.on_click(move || emit(…))` for the click — one declaration each, via `chrome::fires()` :3040. **A pick is not a click**: they are different gestures and a region may answer them differently, so the two closures are deliberately separate and only collapse when the act genuinely is the same (a header button).\n\n⚠️ **This phase used to describe step 2 as `hints.register(InteractionIntent::…)` + `.hint_target(id)`. That API is DELETED** — `HintTargetRegistry`, `HintTargets`, `HintTargetId`, `Base::hint_target` and `named_press` were all removed by F004/P084/T399 under ⭐⭐ RULE ZERO, because a plugin could construct none of them. Do not reintroduce any of them, and do not \"preserve\" hint-id monotonicity: nothing is registered any more, so nothing has to be un-registered when a tree rebuilds. The framework collects the declarations out of the laid-out tree (`heca_grid_ui::collect_peeks`) and runs one (`fire_peek`).\n\nCall sites doing the recipe by hand: `build_pane_header()` :860 (per configured `PaneAction`, via `pane_action_spec()` :652), `sidebar_toggle_button()` :1834, and the overlay's action buttons (`heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs:560`, which already funnels through `action_tooltip`).\n\n## The contract fixed here (T373, landed)\n\n- A component takes **plain data plus the app seams it binds** — `Intent` / `ChromeIntentEmitter`, `&mut BuildCx` (drag, signals), an action **name**, a theme. **Never `&AppState`**: it needs a window, so a component that takes it is a component nobody can test. Same split that made `route_in_domain`, `cursor_follow` and `resolve_context_for` testable.\n- A component **never** spells a shortcut, picks a glyph, or hardcodes a measure. Name the action; the catalog and `ActionShortcuts` answer.\n- **Sizes are shares, never computed pixels** — `Length::Pct` of a shared denominator, or a `grow` weight. A composition that multiplies model numbers by a scale of its own has taken over the layout engine's job and then owns every term (the exposé's seven attempts).\n- **Where it lives**: beside its surface (`heca/src/chrome/<surface>/`) until a **second** surface wants it; the second caller is the move. `heca/src/components/` is the home for the shared case.\n- If a proposed component binds **no** app concept, it is a widget in the wrong crate — send it to `heca-grid-ui` instead.\n\n## Test pattern established (T373)\n\nHeadless, asserting the built tree or the painted scene — not a flag. Follow `heca/src/providers/mod.rs::the_shared_context_carries_nothing_of_one_components_domain` (builds through `ChromeCtx::for_build`, asserts children and what the host registries received) and `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs` (paint into a `Scene`, assert `DrawCommand`s). A component sized by shares also gets the test shares exist for: lay it out in a box and assert it never exceeds it.\n\nFor the action button (T374), assert: the tooltip carries the action's live shortcut, and the click and the pick carry the **same** intent when — and only when — they are the same act.\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\n\nIdentical pixels; identical tooltip text; the existing `pane_action_spec` mapping of `PaneAction` → (glyph, action, label, focus-first) stays the single source of what a header button is.",
  "descriptionUpdatedAt": "2026-07-30T13:27:19.410Z",
