    {
      "id": "bbd49c69-6b48-41cd-9bb9-4b95ef1cd53d",
      "phaseId": "66b0de41-be11-474f-badf-f2b9b934eaf9",
      "number": 374,
      "shortId": "E3U22",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "the-chrome-action-button-becom",
      "title": "The chrome action button becomes a component — one call, not a two-step recipe",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "The first extraction, chosen because it is the composition the app repeats most and the one AGENTS already has to explain step by step.\n\n## What exists\n\nAGENTS § \"Chrome buttons → action, tooltip, KeyHint\" documents a **two-step recipe every caller performs by hand**:\n\n1. `action_tooltip(button, action_name, label, &state.action_shortcuts)` — `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:521` — composes `\"<label>  <shortcut>\"` from the action's **name** (never a hand-picked key string), resolving through `ActionShortcuts` so a rebind updates every tip.\n2. `let hint_id = hints.register(InteractionIntent::…)` then `.hint_target(hint_id)` **and** `.on_click(move || emit(same intent))` — the same intent registered twice, once for the `prefix+/` pick and once for the click, so they can never diverge.\n\nCall sites doing this by hand: `build_pane_header()` :782 (per configured `PaneAction`, whose glyph/action/label/focus-first come from `pane_action_spec()` :549), `sidebar_toggle_button` (the AGENTS-cited complete example), and the overlay's dialog buttons (`heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs:431`).\n\nNote `pane_action_spec` also returns **`needs_focus`**: an active-targeted button (zoom/float — the `WmAction` carries no pane id) must emit `FocusPaneThenAction`, while pane-parameterized ones use `ActivateAction`. The component has to carry that distinction, not flatten it.\n\n## What to build\n\nAn action-button component taking: the action **name**, the `Intent`/`InteractionIntent` it fires, a label, an optional explicit glyph (default: `ActionCatalog::icon(name)`), a `WidgetSize`, and the seams (`&ActionShortcuts`, `&mut BuildCx` for the hint id, the emitter). It returns the tooltip-wrapped, hint-registered, click-wired button as one value.\n\nThen **delete the hand-wiring at every call site above in this same task** — an extraction that leaves the recipe behind has achieved nothing.\n\n## Test (headless, asserts the visible thing)\n\n- The tooltip text carries the action's **live** shortcut from `ActionShortcuts`, and is the label alone when unbound.\n- A hint target was registered, and the intent behind the hint id is **identical** to the one `on_click` emits.\n- With `needs_focus`, the emitted intent is the focus-then-act composite, not the bare action.\n- The glyph comes from the catalog when none is passed.\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\n\nPixel-identical buttons; hint ids stay monotonic and their ranges are still removed when a tree rebuilds (`HintTargetRegistry::remove_range`, see `render.rs` for the chrome tree and `sync_pane_headers` for the per-pane header trees); `pane_action_spec` remains the single source of what a header button is; the config's `[pane] title_actions` (and any future plugin-added button) keeps flowing through the same dynamic vector — never a per-action `match` in the build loop.",
